{"id":"f13t1","name":"Three Systems, One Customer","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Three systems know our customers, and the data team must build one golden record per customer. Each system drops its exports in its own folder of <code>input_dir</code>:</p>\n<p><code>crm/</code> holds CSV files with a header and the columns <code>customer_ref</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>city</code> and <code>updated</code> (<code>yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss</code>). <code>shop/</code> holds JSON lines files where each object looks like <code>{\"email\": ..., \"tel\": ..., \"town\": ..., \"ts\": ...}</code>, <code>ts</code> being a Unix time in seconds. <code>support/</code> holds JSON lines files where each object looks like <code>{\"contact\": {\"mail\": ..., \"phone\": ...}, \"updated_at\": ...}</code>, with an ISO time such as <code>2026-03-01T10:00:00Z</code>; the support tool does not know the city. Files have the extension of their format (<code>.csv</code> or <code>.jsonl</code>); anything else is ignored. All times are UTC.</p>\n<p>Customers are matched by email only, after trimming it and putting it in lower case; a record whose email does not contain <code>@</code> cannot be matched and is dropped. Phone numbers are typed in every possible way (<code>+212 6 12-34-56-78</code>, <code>0612345678</code>, <code>(212) 612 345 678</code>): keep only the digits, then remove a leading <code>212</code> country code if there is one, then a leading <code>0</code>; what remains is the phone. City names are trimmed and written in title case (<code>casablanca</code> becomes <code>Casablanca</code>). An empty or missing value is not a value.</p>\n<p>For each field, the golden record takes the value of the <b>most recent</b> record (by update time, whatever the system) that has a value for this field. If two records with a value have exactly the same time, any of them is fine because they always agree in the tests.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per customer with the columns <code>email</code>, <code>phone</code>, <code>city</code> (strings, <code>null</code> if no record has a value) and <code>systems</code> (long, number of the three systems in which the customer appears), sorted by <code>email</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/crm/2026/a.csv</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">customer_ref,email,phone,city,updated\nC0, Ana@Mail.com,0612345678,casablanca,2026-03-01 09:00:00\nC1,bob@x.io,, rabat ,2026-03-01 09:00:00\nC2,no-email,0611,fes,2026-03-01 09:00:00\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/shop/s.jsonl</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"email\": \"ana@mail.com\", \"tel\": \"+212 6 99-88-77-66\", \"town\": \"\", \"ts\": 1772445600}\n{\"email\": \"bob@x.io\", \"tel\": \"0655555555\", \"town\": \"Tanger\", \"ts\": 1769940000}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/support/t.jsonl</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"contact\": {\"mail\": \"ANA@mail.com \", \"phone\": \"(212) 611 111 111\"}, \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-15T08:00:00Z\"}\n{\"contact\": {\"mail\": \"cy@z.ma\", \"phone\": \"0700000000\"}, \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-03T12:00:00Z\"}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/support/old.json</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{}\n</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>email</th><th>phone</th><th>city</th><th>systems</th></tr><tr><td>ana@mail.com</td><td>699887766</td><td>Casablanca</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>bob@x.io</td><td>655555555</td><td>Rabat</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>cy@z.ma</td><td>700000000</td><td>null</td><td>1</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"import os\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return spark.read.json(os.path.join(input_dir, \"shop\"))\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["consigne longue","CSV et JSON mélangés","normalisation","dernière valeur non vide par champ"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"crm/2026/a.csv":"customer_ref,email,phone,city,updated\nC0, Ana@Mail.com,0612345678,casablanca,2026-03-01 09:00:00\nC1,bob@x.io,, rabat ,2026-03-01 09:00:00\nC2,no-email,0611,fes,2026-03-01 09:00:00\n","shop/s.jsonl":"{\"email\": \"ana@mail.com\", \"tel\": \"+212 6 99-88-77-66\", \"town\": \"\", \"ts\": 1772445600}\n{\"email\": \"bob@x.io\", \"tel\": \"0655555555\", \"town\": \"Tanger\", \"ts\": 1769940000}\n","support/t.jsonl":"{\"contact\": {\"mail\": \"ANA@mail.com \", \"phone\": \"(212) 611 111 111\"}, \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-15T08:00:00Z\"}\n{\"contact\": {\"mail\": \"cy@z.ma\", \"phone\": \"0700000000\"}, \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-03T12:00:00Z\"}\n","support/old.json":"{}\n"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"crm/2026/a.csv":"customer_ref,email,phone,city,updated\nC0, Ana@Mail.com,0612345678,casablanca,2026-03-01 09:00:00\nC1,bob@x.io,, rabat ,2026-03-01 09:00:00\nC2,no-email,0611,fes,2026-03-01 09:00:00\n","shop/s.jsonl":"{\"email\": \"ana@mail.com\", \"tel\": \"+212 6 99-88-77-66\", \"town\": \"\", \"ts\": 1772445600}\n{\"email\": \"bob@x.io\", \"tel\": \"0655555555\", \"town\": \"Tanger\", \"ts\": 1769940000}\n","support/t.jsonl":"{\"contact\": {\"mail\": \"ANA@mail.com \", \"phone\": \"(212) 611 111 111\"}, \"updated_at\": \"2026-02-15T08:00:00Z\"}\n{\"contact\": {\"mail\": \"cy@z.ma\", \"phone\": \"0700000000\"}, \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-03T12:00:00Z\"}\n","support/old.json":"{}\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["email","phone","city","systems"],"rows":[["ana@mail.com","699887766","Casablanca",3],["bob@x.io","655555555","Rabat",2],["cy@z.ma","700000000",null,1]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"shop/a.jsonl":"{\"email\": \"d@d.d\", \"tel\": \"0600000001\", \"town\": \"agadir\", \"ts\": 1767225600}\n{\"email\": \"d@d.d\", \"tel\": \"0600000002\", \"town\": null, 